new file mode 100644
index 00000000..739a2593
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/subsys/425-wifi-mac80211-clear-the-Critical-Update-flag-after-t.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,429 @@
+From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
+Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: clear the Critical Update flag after the
+ DTIM Beacon
+
+mac80211 sends the beacon head of user space as it is, so the Critical
+Update flag stays in the Beacon frames until user space updates the
+beacon. User space cannot see the DTIM Beacon frame that ends the flag
+(IEEE 802.11be-2024 35.3.10).
+
+Track the flag for each link of an AP MLD. A beacon update that sets it
+with a new critical update ID, or while no critical update runs, starts
+it, and the next DTIM Beacon frame of the link ends it. For Beacon
+frames from ieee80211_beacon_get(), mac80211 sees the DTIM Count it
+writes. A driver that builds Beacon frames from a template calls the new
+ieee80211_crit_update_done() when the device sent the DTIM Beacon frame.
+It passes the critical update ID that ieee80211_beacon_get_template()
+reported for the template of that Beacon frame, so that a late report of
+an older critical update does not end a newer one. From then on,
+mac80211 clears the flag in the Beacon frames and in the template,
+updates the beacon of the driver and sends NL80211_CMD_CRIT_UPDATE_DONE
+with the ID. The flag stays out until user space updates the beacon
+without it or with a new ID, because user space can update the beacon
+with the flag of the same critical update before it reads the event.
+
+Each beacon holds the critical update that it belongs to. A Beacon
+frame that mac80211 builds from a beacon while a beacon update replaces
+it neither ends nor clears the flag of the critical update of the new
+beacon.
+
+A nontransmitted BSSID has no Beacon frames of its own, so mac80211
+does not track its flag and reports no event for it.
+
+cfg80211_beacon_dup() copies the critical update ID, so that the beacon
+after a channel switch or a colour change keeps the ID that user space
+gave for it.
+
+Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
