+From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
+Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:00:01 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: match SCS descriptors on their client address
+
+An SCS descriptor can name a client behind a 4-address peer, but
+cfg80211_scs_evaluate() matches it against every MSDU sent to the peer.
+The descriptor of one host thus classifies the flows of every other
+host behind the same peer.
+
+Only match a descriptor with a client against an MSDU whose destination
+address equals it. The client is not a classifier parameter and does
+not count towards the granularity of a descriptor.
+
+Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
+
