+From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
+Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:00:03 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: keep an MSCS per client and configured flag
+
+A station holds one MSCS. ieee80211_flow_learn() only learns frames
+whose source address is the station's own, and the learned priority
+applies to every MSDU sent to the station. On a 4-address peer, the
+uplink of a host behind it is never learned, and an MSCS for one host
+replaces that of another.
+
+Keep a list of MSCS per station, identified by the client address and
+the configured flag. An MSCS without a client mirrors the flows of the
+station itself, as before. Each MSCS learns from uplink MSDUs whose
+source address is its client and applies to downlink MSDUs whose
+destination address is its client, with entries of its own. The MSCS
+that the station requested come first in the list, so that one of them
+wins over a configured one for the same MSDU, as Wi-Fi EasyMesh 6.0,
+20.2.5 requires. A station holds at most 16 MSCS, and a request beyond
+that is declined.
+
+The MSCS debugfs file lists every MSCS of the station, and the SCS file
+shows the client of a rule.
+
+Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
