--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/subsys/475-wifi-mac80211-mark-frames-whose-priority-does-not-fo.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,103 @@
+From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
+Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:30:00 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: mark frames whose priority does not follow the DSCP
+
+A device that encapsulates 802.3 frames in firmware can take the TID of
+a frame from its DSCP with a mapping of its own. A frame whose priority
+mac80211 did not take from the DSCP with the RFC 8325 default is then
+sent with another TID. This applies to a priority of 256 to 263 set
+before the frame reaches mac80211, a VLAN PCP, a QoS map of the
+interface and an SCS or MSCS rule.
+
+Mark such frames with IEEE80211_TX_CTRL_EXPLICIT_UP, so that a driver
+can hand skb->priority to the device for them. Compare after the
+downgrade for admission control, which can change the priority as well.
+A frame without a DSCP is expected at priority 0.
+cfg80211_classify8021d() gives an 802.21 frame priority 7 and an MPLS
+frame the traffic class of its label, so these frames are marked unless
+their priority is 0.
+
+Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
+
